         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Journal Line as its primary object. A data source filter is required to be selected prior to running reports. The filters use Reporting Time Periods so that reports can be designed based on relative time spans.\nThe results will only include journal lines for journals that are in Posted or Proforma status, e.g. it automatically excludes journals that have been cancelled or are in error or draft status. This Data Source has the ability to create derived Journal Lines for financial reporting calculations similar to amounts reported by Trial Balance or Financial Statement. The derived journal lines can include system calculated amounts for currency translation gain or loss, Intercompany and Interworktag Eliminations and Eliminations Variance, and aggregated Current Year Retained Earnings.",
         "Data_Source_Filter": "Journal Lines for Company and Reporting Time Period",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Cost Center; Cash Flow Code; Ledger Account; Company; Translated Debit Amount; Spend Category as Worktag; Translated Credit Amount; Revenue Category",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Journal; Cost Center; Book Codes IN Book  for RDS Filter; Accounting Date; Ledger Account; Cash Flow Code; Customer Contract as Worktag; Transaction Currency; Book Codes Not In Book for RDS Filter; Intercompany Affiliate; Period; Journal Status; Company; Translated Debit Amount; Year; Translation Currency; Translated Credit Amount; Supplier as Worktag; Sales Item; Book Code; Pay Component; Campus; Job Profile; Division; Campaign; Business Document; Line of Business; Worktags; Location; Bank Account; Customer; Journal Source; Expense Item as Worktag; Project; Worker; Region; Spend Category as Worktag; Revenue Category",
         "Report_Name": "Sub Report - Journal Lines Translated Debit Credit Summation Fields",
         "Report_Owner": "tserrano / Teresa Serrano",
         "Report_Type": "Matrix",
         "Used_in_Composite_Report_Definition": "Trial Balance with CTA",
         "referenceID": "Journal Lines for Financial Reporting"
      },
      {
         "Brief_Description": "An employee directory grouped and outlined by Supervisory Organization.",
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Worker as its primary object and returns one row per worker. This data source will show all active and terminated workers, regardless of contextual security. For active workers, all fields are as of the current date or Effective Date, if specified. For terminated workers, all fields are always as of the last day of work. Does not contain any built-in prompts. This data source can be used to build reports for only active and terminated workers and not all workers. For better performance, use the Indexed Worker data source instead. To identify if a worker is active or terminated, use the Currently Active field. This field will return whether the worker is active as of the current date.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Manager - Level 01; Worker; Group Name; Supervisory Organization; Total Base Pay Annualized in Reporting Currency - Amount; Photo; Compa-Ratio; One",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Manager - Level 01; Worker; Group Name; Supervisory Organization; Organization; Level 04 from the Top; Worker Active; Total Base Pay Annualized in Reporting Currency - Amount; Level 03 from the Top; Photo; Worker is Employee; Compa-Ratio; One",
         "Report_Name": "Supervisory Headcount Outlined Report",
         "Report_Owner": "lmcneil / Logan McNeil",
         "Report_Type": "Advanced",
         "referenceID": "All Active and Terminated Workers"
      },
