      {
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Action Event as its primary business object and returns business process transactions for all business process types.\n\nIncludes optional prompts for: Business Processes, Completed Date Range, Event Effective Date Range, Initiated Date Range, and Transaction Status.\n\nWorkday highly recommends that you use the Business Processes, Transaction Status, and date range (Initiated Date Range or Completed Date Range) as required prompts because this improves the performance of your report.\n\nThis report data source doesn't include outbound records for Staffing events that move workers from 1 organization to another. It only includes inbound records for this type of event.\n\nConsider using event report data sources for specific functional areas if you're trying to access data within those events. Example: A report navigates to data using calculated fields as a prompt or filter.\n\nIf you need to filter by or report on individual step details, use the Business Process Event Steps report data source.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Action Event",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Cancelable; Action Event",
         "Report_Name": "MOM Cancel BP Input Report",
         "Report_Owner": "lmcneil / Logan McNeil",
         "Report_Type": "Advanced",
         "referenceID": "Business Process Transactions"
      },
      {
         "DS_Description": "Accesses business process step-level information. The Business Process Event Steps object accesses one row per Business Process Event Step including Completed By or Awaiting Workers, Event Record Actions, and related Business Process Event information.\n\nIncludes optional prompts for: Business Process Type, Event Record Actions, and Workers.\n\nPrompts you for required prompts: Start and end dates when the user took action on the step.\n\nThis report data source doesn't return event records that kick-off a sub-event.\n\nWorkday highly recommends that you use the Business Process Type, Event Record Actions, and date range (Initiated Date Range or Completed Date Range) as required prompts because this improves the performance of your report. Create the prompts using non-indexed report fields.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Event Record",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Event Record; Reassignable Step With Awaiting Persons (Do Not Use)",
         "Report_Name": "MOM Reassign Input Report",
         "Report_Owner": "lmcneil / Logan McNeil",
         "Report_Type": "Advanced",
         "referenceID": "Business Process Event Steps"
      },
      {
         "DS_Description": "Accesses business process step-level information. The Business Process Event Steps object accesses one row per Business Process Event Step including Completed By or Awaiting Workers, Event Record Actions, and related Business Process Event information.\n\nIncludes optional prompts for: Business Process Type, Event Record Actions, and Workers.\n\nPrompts you for required prompts: Start and end dates when the user took action on the step.\n\nThis report data source doesn't return event records that kick-off a sub-event.\n\nWorkday highly recommends that you use the Business Process Type, Event Record Actions, and date range (Initiated Date Range or Completed Date Range) as required prompts because this improves the performance of your report. Create the prompts using non-indexed report fields.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Event Record",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Step Can Escalate; Event Record",
         "Report_Name": "MOM Escalate Input Report",
         "Report_Owner": "lmcneil / Logan McNeil",
         "Report_Type": "Advanced",
         "referenceID": "Business Process Event Steps"
      },
      {
         "Brief_Description": "View the reports delivered by Workday, report type, whether it can be scheduled, and the domain in which it is secured. Enables you to see whether a report can be copied and customized (Report Writer type reports only). This report does not include reports that are only available as a related action or that only serve to initiate a task.\n\nRequired prompt: Report Categories\nOptional prompt: none",
         "DS_Description": "Returns the categories associated with Workday-delivered reports. Prompts for one or more categories. If none are provided, all report categories are returned.",
