      {
         "Brief_Description": "This report displays Headcount by Country based on the International Assignment Type.\nIf the assignment is Long Term or Indefinite, headcount is automatically counted in Host Country.\nIf the assignment is Short Term, headcount is automatically counted in Home Country.",
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Worker as its primary object and returns one row per worker. This data source will show all active and terminated workers, regardless of contextual security. For active workers, all fields are as of the current date or Effective Date, if specified. For terminated workers, all fields are always as of the last day of work. Does not contain any built-in prompts. This data source can be used to build reports for only active and terminated workers and not all workers. For better performance, use the Indexed Worker data source instead. To identify if a worker is active or terminated, use the Currently Active field. This field will return whether the worker is active as of the current date.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Country for Headcount",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Manager - Level 01; Worker; Supervisory Organization; Country; Currently Active; Effective Date for Position; Cost Center; All Positions / Jobs; Position; Gender; International Assignment & Secondment Types; Location; Job Profile; Primary Job; Supervisory Manager; Location; Worker Type; Supervisory Organization; Is International Assignment & Secondment; Position - Filled; Position - Position Management; Home Position (As of Date); Work Address - Country",
         "Report_Name": "Headcount by Country (based on International Assignment Type)",
         "Report_Owner": "lmcneil / Logan McNeil",
         "Report_Type": "Matrix",
         "referenceID": "All Active and Terminated Workers"
      },
      {
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Worker as its primary object and returns one row per worker. This data source will show all active and terminated workers, regardless of contextual security. Includes all workers even workers to be hired in the future. Doesn't contain any built-in prompts. This data source can be used to build reports on all workers. Helpful Tips: 1) If the worker is hired in the future, all fields will be returned based on the effective date. 2) If no effective date is specified, the system will use the current date as the effective date. 3) If the effective date is less than the worker's hire date, no effective dated information (such as position information, compensation information and so on) will be returned. 4) If effective dated behavior is desired, use the All Active and Terminated Workers data source instead.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Worker; Overtime Risk",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Last Day of This Week; Worker; Prompt - Date 1; End Date; Start Date; Prompt - Date 2; Calculation Tags; Calculated Quantity; Time Blocks for Worker; First Day of This Month",
         "Report_Name": "JPN Alert - Overtime Risk",
         "Report_Owner": "lmcneil / Logan McNeil",
         "Report_Type": "Advanced",
         "referenceID": "All Workers"
      },
      {
