      {
         "Brief_Description": "Benchmark vs. Actual Report for Diversity & Inclusion Data",
         "DS_Description": "The Benchmark Values data source accesses the Benchmark Values object and returns one row per unique combination of dimension values and benchmarks. Includes built-in prompts for Benchmark Functional Area, Benchmark Subcategory, Group by Dimension, and Benchmarking dimensions Industry Group, Industry, Size, Workday Tenure, Country, Worker Type, and Gender. This data source returns benchmarking results for the latest period in which data is available.\n\nFor any report that’s built on this data source, Workday precalculates and displays benchmarking percentile data based on participant thresholding criteria. Workday displays:\n1. No percentile data for a row when the number of participants is less than 6.\n2. Data only for the 25th, 50th and 75th percentiles when the number of participants is from 6 to 11, inclusive.\n3. Data for all 5 percentiles when the number of participants is greater than 11.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Benchmark; Benchmark Subcategory; Period; Benchmark Category; Industry Group; Workday Tenure (Years); Size (Employees); Country; 10th Percentile; 50th Percentile; 90th Percentile; Actual Value; 25th Percentile; Number of Participants; 75th Percentile; Worker Type; Gender; Absence Policy; Industry; Benchmark Type",
