      {
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Action Event as its primary business object and returns business process transactions for all business process types.\n\nIncludes optional prompts for: Business Processes, Completed Date Range, Event Effective Date Range, Initiated Date Range, and Transaction Status.\n\nWorkday highly recommends that you use the Business Processes, Transaction Status, and date range (Initiated Date Range or Completed Date Range) as required prompts because this improves the performance of your report.\n\nThis report data source doesn't include outbound records for Staffing events that move workers from 1 organization to another. It only includes inbound records for this type of event.\n\nConsider using event report data sources for specific functional areas if you're trying to access data within those events. Example: A report navigates to data using calculated fields as a prompt or filter.\n\nIf you need to filter by or report on individual step details, use the Business Process Event Steps report data source.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Worker Location; Business Process Type",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Business Process Event; Current Worker; Days Past Due; Awaiting Persons; Used in Payroll Interface; Current Effective Date; Last Day of This Month; Supervisory Organization; Pay Group (Do Not Use); Business Process Transaction; Worker Business Process; Comments; Workday ID; Organization Type; First Day of This Month; Is True; Initiator; Organizations and Subordinates (Static Prompt); Current Period in Progress; Organization; Due Date; Date and Time Initiated; Run Category; Subject; Pay Group; Business Process; Effective Date; Business Process Type; Worker; Workers That Completed Most Recent Step; Location; Role Name; Organization; Workers; Organization Role Assignments; Next Period to Process; Pay Group (Do Not Use); Performed by; About Worker; Days Past Due Range; Transaction Status",
         "Report_Name": "BP Transactions related to current pay period",
         "Report_Owner": "agarcia / Alex Garcia",
         "Report_Type": "Matrix",
         "referenceID": "Business Process Transactions"
      },
      {
         "Brief_Description": "This matrix report enables payroll partners to view aggregated pay components by establishment, and in a similar format as the payslip. The report splits contributions by rates. The report uses the Pay Components Combined report data source.",
         "DS_Description": "Accesses Pay Component (Combined) DI as the primary business object and returns 1 row per group of employee and employer pay component and per payroll result. Excludes pay component combinations where both the employee and employer pay components have a result of 0. Includes all results when you select the Allow display on payslip when equal to 0 check box on the Maintain Earnings and Deductions Reporting Order task. Prompts you for these values to automatically filter the report results:\n* Companies with SIREN\n* Pay Run Groups and/or Pay Group Details\n* Periods\n* Establishments\n* Pay Components\n* Pay Cycle Type\n* Payment Date From\n* Payment Date To",
