      {
         "Brief_Description": "View all the approved, pending, and denied time off requests for your workers to track the history and status of all time off requests. Leave one or both dates blank to perform an open-ended search. The report lists worker time off for one or more organizations where the worker's Time Off Date falls on or within the specified date range. Additional details include time off type, dates entered and approved, date off, and hours. Enables you to perform related actions to manage time off and leave for individual workers.  \n\nRequired prompt: Organizations\nOptional prompts: Include Subordinate Organizations, Start Date, End Date",
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Time Off Entry as its primary object.  The Time Off Entry object returns one row per time off line item an worker has requested.  Includes all time off (including approved, pending and denied) for workers in organizations which the user manages or supports.  Prompts the user at run-time for Organization, Include Subordinate, and Date Range on paid time date taken to automatically filter the report results. If the worker is not eligible for the time off as of the dates entered, they will not appear on the report (termination causes worker to be ineligible).",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Out Time; In Time; Time Off Entry; Position; Time Off/Absence Table; Worker Employee ID; Units Pending; Unit of Time; Units Approved; Units Denied; Organization as of the Time Off Date; Request or Correction; Approval Date; Time Off Type for Time Off Entry; Time Off Reason; Entered On; Worker; Time Off Date",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Out Time; In Time; Time Off Entry; Position; Employee ID; Time Off/Absence Table; Worker; Units Pending; Unit of Time; Units Approved; Units Denied; Organization as of the Time Off Date; Request or Correction; Approval Date; Time Off Type for Time Off Entry; Time Off Reason; Entered On; Worker; Time Off Date",
         "Report_Name": "All Worker Time Off",
         "Report_Owner": "agarcia / Alex Garcia",
         "Report_Type": "Advanced",
         "referenceID": "Time Off by Date Taken"
      },
      {
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Leave of Absence Requests as its primary object.  The Leave Requests object returns one row per worker leave.  Includes all approved and pending (if Include Pending Events is true) worker leave requests where the actual last day of leave is not in the date range and the first day of leave is before the end date for organizations which the user manages or supports.  If the Include Workers Returned from Leave is checked on the leave requests returned will also include leave requests where the first day of leave is within the date range and the actual last day of leave is not considered.   Prompts the user at run-time for Organization, Include Subordinate, Include Pending Events, Date Ranges and Include Workers Returned from Leave to automatically filter the report results.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Status; Last Day of Leave - Actual; Leave Type (Including Family); Last Day of Leave - Estimated; First Day of Leave; Last Day of Work; First Day Back at Work; Worker; Date and Time Completed; Total Days on Leave; Employee ID",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Status; Last Day of Leave - Actual; Leave Type (Including Family); Last Day of Leave - Estimated; First Day of Leave; Last Day of Work; First Day Back at Work; Worker; Employee ID; Date and Time Completed; Total Days on Leave",
         "Report_Name": "Leave Of Absence Overview",
         "Report_Owner": "agarcia / Alex Garcia",
         "Report_Type": "Advanced",
         "referenceID": "Leave of Absence Outstanding by Date Range"
      },
