         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Action Event as its primary business object and returns business process transactions for all business process types. Only administrators on the Business Process Administration domain can access data being returned.\n\nIncludes an optional prompt for Business Process Name.\n\nIncludes additional indexed fields for filtering that can be helpful: About Worker, Action Has Target Organization, Date and Time Completed, Date and Time Initiated, Initiating Worker, and Transaction Status.\n\nWorkday highly recommends that you use the Business Process Name, Transaction Status, and date range (Initiated Date Range or Completed Date Range) as required prompts because this improves the performance of your report. Create the prompts using non-indexed report fields.\n\nThis report data source doesn't include outbound records for Staffing events that move workers from 1 organization to another. It only includes inbound records for this type of event.\n\nConsider using event report data sources for specific functional areas if you're trying to access data within those events. Example: A report navigates to data using calculated fields as a prompt or filter.",
