         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Positions as its primary object.  The Position object returns one row per position.  Includes all filled positions, open position restrictions, and closed position restrictions. Each position is evaluated using an effective date set to 1) current date if not closed or 2) availability date or 3) close date. That is, if the position restrictions is closed, the display of the position restrictions will show the wording \"Closed\". Does not contain any built-in prompts. \nPositions returned will only include the ones that the login user can access.\n\nWhen creating a custom report to return specific positions, we recommend that you use these high-performance report data sources instead: Positions from ID, and Positions for HCM Reporting.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Worker Type; Position ID; Worker; Position Text; Availability Date; Hiring Restrictions - Location; Worker; Position - Position Management; Hiring Restrictions - Position Worker Type; Available For Hire; Location",
