         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Worker as its primary object and returns one row per worker. This data source will show all active and terminated workers, regardless of contextual security. For active workers, all fields are as of the current date or Effective Date, if specified. For terminated workers, all fields are always as of the last day of work. Does not contain any built-in prompts. This data source can be used to build reports for only active and terminated workers and not all workers. For better performance, use the Indexed Worker data source instead. To identify if a worker is active or terminated, use the Currently Active field. This field will return whether the worker is active as of the current date.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Worker; Average Weekly Paid Hours Based On Affordable Care Act; Average Monthly Paid Hours Based On Affordable Care Act; Employee ID; Measurement Period Type; Average ACA Hours Per Month; Hire Date; ACA Measurement Period Worker History Instances; Average ACA Hours Per Week; Qualified As Full-time Based On ACA Measurement Period; Stability Period Start Date; Stability Period End Date; Qualified As ACA FT; Measurement Period Start Date; Measurement Period End Date; Employee; Measurement Period",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Worker; Average Weekly Paid Hours Based On Affordable Care Act; Average Monthly Paid Hours Based On Affordable Care Act; Organization Assignments; Employee ID; Measurement Period Type; Average ACA Hours Per Month; Hire Date; ACA Measurement Period Worker History Instances; Compensation Plan; Average ACA Hours Per Week; Qualified As Full-time Based On ACA Measurement Period; Stability Period Start Date; Stability Period End Date; Qualified As ACA FT; Measurement Period Start Date; Measurement Period End Date; Compensation Plans Effective; Employee; Measurement Period; Scheduled Weekly Hours",
