      {
         "Brief_Description": "This sub report is used in the Balance Sheet composite report.  It queries from the Journal Lines for Financial Reporting data source.",
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Journal Line as its primary object. A data source filter is required to be selected prior to running reports. The filters use Reporting Time Periods so that reports can be designed based on relative time spans.\nThe results will only include journal lines for journals that are in Posted or Proforma status, e.g. it automatically excludes journals that have been cancelled or are in error or draft status. This Data Source has the ability to create derived Journal Lines for financial reporting calculations similar to amounts reported by Trial Balance or Financial Statement. The derived journal lines can include system calculated amounts for currency translation gain or loss, Intercompany and Interworktag Eliminations and Eliminations Variance, and aggregated Current Year Retained Earnings.",
         "Data_Source_Filter": "Journal Lines for Company and Reporting Time Period",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Cost Center; Ledger Account; Translated Debit Minus Credit Amount; Company; Spend Category as Worktag; Bank Account; Revenue Category",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Journal; Cost Center; Book Codes IN Book  for RDS Filter; Accounting Date; Ledger Account; Investor; Transaction Currency; Book Codes Not In Book for RDS Filter; Intercompany Affiliate; Investment Pool; Period; Sponsor; Journal Status; Translated Debit Minus Credit Amount; Company; Year; Translation Currency; Gift; Sales Item; Book Code; Business Unit; Grant; Pay Component; Worktags; Location; Bank Account; Customer; Ledger/Budget Period; Journal Source; Fund; Expense Item as Worktag; Project; Region; Spend Category as Worktag; Revenue Category",
         "Report_Name": "PB_Income_Statement-Sub Report - Journal Lines Translated for Financial Reports",
         "Report_Owner": "Pbhivandkar-trn / Bhivandkar Pratik J",
         "Report_Type": "Matrix",
         "Used_in_Composite_Report_Definition": "PB_Income_Statement",
         "referenceID": "Journal Lines for Financial Reporting"
      },
      {
         "Brief_Description": "This composite report allows you to view an Income Statement for a Company or Company Hierarchy. The Income Statement uses the Journal Lines for Financial Reporting data source and compares YTD Actuals against Prior YTD Actuals.  The rows in this report are defined using Workday owned Aliases.  In order to run this report you must run the task: Map Standard Aliases and map ALL of the Alias values defined in this report. \n\nRequired prompts: Company, Ledger, Period, Translation Currency, Account Translation Rule Set.\n\nOptional prompts: Book, Balancing Worktags, Worktags, Additional Options",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Today",
         "Report_Name": "PB_Income_Statement",
         "Report_Owner": "Pbhivandkar-trn / Bhivandkar Pratik J",
         "Report_Type": "Composite",
         "Sub-Reports": "PB_Income_Statement-Sub Report - Journal Lines Translated for Financial Reports"
      },
