      {
         "Brief_Description": "Returns new hire employees and contingent workers along with their employee id, hire date, manager, supervisory org and business site.",
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Worker as its primary object and returns one row per worker. This data source will show all active and terminated workers, regardless of contextual security. For active workers, all fields are as of the current date or Effective Date, if specified. For terminated workers, all fields are always as of the last day of work. Does not contain any built-in prompts. This data source can be used to build reports for only active and terminated workers and not all workers. For better performance, use the Indexed Worker data source instead. To identify if a worker is active or terminated, use the Currently Active field. This field will return whether the worker is active as of the current date.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Manager - Level 01; Hire Date; Management Level; Worker; Supervisory Organization; Dependents; Legal Name; Age; Compensation Grade; Relationship; Job Profile; Location",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Manager - Level 01; Active Status; Worker; Dependents; Age; Today; Relationship; Job Profile; Location; Hire Date; Management Level; -1; Supervisory Organization; Legal Name; 1; Compensation Grade",
         "Report_Name": "voruganti-trn New Hire Summary",
         "Report_Owner": "voruganti-trn / Vishal Oruganti",
         "Report_Type": "Advanced",
         "referenceID": "All Active and Terminated Workers"
      },
      {
         "DS_Description": "Accesses the Employee as its primary object and returns one row per employee. Only includes active workers associated with the supervisory organizations the user manages. Contains the following Built-in-prompts: Include Managers, Include Subordinate Organizations, and Organization. This data source can be used to build reports on active workers. Helpful Tip: Only Workers who belong to one of the following are returned: employees associated with the supervisory organizations selected, employees associated with the corresponding subordinate organizations if you select Include Subordinate Organizations, or the manager associated with each supervisory and subordinate organization included if you select Include Managers.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Expense Report; Expense Reports - All Statuses; Supervisory Organization; Employee; Expense Items on Expense Report; Expense Report Total Amount; Location",
         "Fields_Referenced_in_Report": "Expense Reports - All Statuses; Expense Report; Supervisory Organization; Employee; Expense Items on Expense Report; Expense Report Total Amount; Location",
