      {
         "Brief_Description": "View employees who are eligible to progress to the next compensation step in their grade but did not because a parallel compensation process was in progress at the same time as the automatic step progression process. The automatic step progression process can advance employees to the next step only if there are no parallel compensation processes in progress. Note that merit is not excluded as a parallel compensation process in progress.\n\nClick the Parallel Compensation Process link to drill to the compensation event that prevented the step progression. You can then complete the processing of that conflicting compensation event for the pending employee and rerun the automatic step progression process. You can use the Schedule a Report task to schedule the report to run at the same time as automatic step progression process. \n\nRequired prompt: none\nOptional prompt: none",
         "DS_Description": "Find Employee Positions which will be eligible for a new Compensation Step between today and a Future Date.",
         "Fields_Displayed_on_Report": "Compensation Grade Profile; Compensation Grade; Position; Union for Position; Compensation Step - Next; Compensation Step - Current; Photo; Worker; Parallel Compensation Processes; Compensation Step - Next Start Date; Compensation Step - Progression Rule",
